## Correction 1 — round 1 misclassified red 03

Round 1: "03,04 are genuine reds against pre-implementation DOM
(behaviours 3,4)."

04 is genuine: `.fasti-strip` was absent from the DOM.

03 is NOT. Its call log resolves the locator to
`<div data-focused="false" class="inbox__row inbox__row--attention">` — the
rows and the data-focused attribute already rendered, and j/k already
worked. It is red only because the assertion at line 39 read
`toHaveAttribute("data-focused", "true")` where the shipped test reads
`"false"`. That is a mutated-assertion red, same class as 01/02/05.

So the true split is 4 mutated-assertion reds (01,02,03,05) and 2 app-side
reds (04,06 — the same FastiStrip regression, before and after commit).
The reds remain honest; the classification was wrong, and it matters because
a mutated-assertion red proves only that the assertion executes, not that
the suite detects a real regression.

